=== Chicken CO_Mega model (chicken liver) ===

[1] Parsing chicken CDS FASTA into a CSV table...
  Parsed 7,262 CDS records from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/chicken_CDS_sequence.txt
  Saved to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/chicken_CDS_sequence.csv

[2] Computing codon frequencies from CDS sequences...
  Loaded 7,262 genes from /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/data/chicken_CDS_sequence.csv
  Dropped 0 genes with missing/unusable CDS sequences (not a multiple of 3, or too short); 7,262 genes remain.
  6,882 autosomal (chr 1-39) genes, 380 Z-linked genes.
  Saved codon frequencies to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/chicken/codon_frequencies_chicken_liver.csv

[3] Loading canonical chicken liver TE data (EnsemblBioMart IDs already attached)...
  7,678 chicken genes with both TE_mean and a mapped EnsemblBioMart ID in /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_riboseq/tables/chicken_liver/translational_efficiency_data_with_ids.csv (3,722 rows there had no mapped ID -- no clean 1:1 crosswalk mapping -- and are excluded).
  [join audit] chicken codon frequencies (training genes) (7,262 rows, key='te_gene_id') x chicken TE (with EnsemblBioMart IDs) (7,678 rows, key='te_gene_id'):
    duplicated keys: 0 in chicken codon frequencies (training genes), 0 in chicken TE (with EnsemblBioMart IDs)
    unmatched: 3,622 chicken codon frequencies (training genes) keys with no match in chicken TE (with EnsemblBioMart IDs); 4,038 chicken TE (with EnsemblBioMart IDs) keys with no match in chicken codon frequencies (training genes)
    rows after merge ('inner'): 3,640
    Saved unmatched-key audit (7,660 rows) to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/chicken/join_audit_codon_vs_te_train_chicken_liver.csv
  3,640 genes with both codon frequencies and TE_mean.

[4] Fitting TE_mean ~ codon frequencies on autosomal genes...
  Training on 3,436 autosomal genes, 61 codon predictors.
  R^2 = 0.3916   Adjusted R^2 = 0.3808   n = 3436
  Saved intercept + 61 codon coefficients to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/chicken/co_mega_model_coefficients_chicken_liver.csv
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/chicken/co_mega_regression_fit_train_chicken_liver.png  (Pearson R = 0.6258, Pearson R² = 0.3916, p = 6.218e-373, n = 3,436)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/chicken/co_mega_regression_fit_train_spearman_chicken_liver.png  (Spearman rho = 0.6338, Spearman rho² = 0.4017, p = 1.944e-385, n = 3,436)

[4b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Chicken liver) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=3,436): skew = -0.692, excess kurtosis = 0.532, D'Agostino K^2 p = 7.86e-56, Jarque-Bera p = 4.45e-69
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.759, excess kurtosis = 1.509, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.44e-83, Jarque-Bera p = 3.84e-143
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 171.051, p = 2.24e-12
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 8.598, p = 0.000189
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/chicken/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_te_histogram_chicken_liver.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/chicken/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_histogram_chicken_liver.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/chicken/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_qq_chicken_liver.png
  Saved: /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/figures/chicken/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_residual_vs_fitted_chicken_liver.png
  Saved diagnostic statistics to /lab/solexa_page/xueqi/analysis_codon/tables/chicken/co_mega_regression_diagnostics_stats_chicken_liver.csv

